"1693.1","It was narrated to me by Yahya, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from Aslam, the freed slave of Umar ibn al-Khattab, that Umar ibn al-Khattab ruled that a molar tooth incurs a camel, and a collarbone incurs a camel, and a rib incurs a camel."
"1693.2","From Yahya ibn Sa'id, that Umar ibn al-Khattab was eating bread with ghee. He invited a man from the desert, and he began to eat, following the morsel with the edge of the dish. Umar said: It is as if you are destitute. He said: By Allah, I have not eaten ghee, nor have I seen anyone eat with it, for such and such a time. Umar said: I will not eat ghee until people are well-provided for from the beginning of their sustenance."
"1694.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Wahb ibn Kaysan that Jabir ibn Abdullah said"
