"1709.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Sadaqa ibn Yasar said"
"1709.2","When a servant falls ill, Allah the Exalted sends two angels to him and says: ""Look at what he says to his visitors."" If, when they come to him, he praises Allah and extols Him, they raise that to Allah Almighty—and He knows best—and He says: ""It is incumbent upon Me that if I take his soul, I will admit him to Paradise, and if I cure him, I will replace his flesh with better flesh and his blood with better blood, and I will expiate his sins."""
"1710.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr from Abbad ibn Tamim that Abu Bashir al-Ansari told him that he was with the Messenger of Allah"
"1710.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr from Abbad ibn Tamim that Abu Bashir al-Ansari told him that he was with the Messenger of Allah"
"1711.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abi Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf heard his father say"
"1711.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abi Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf heard his father say"
"1712.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Umar ibn Husayn, the mawla of
A'isha bint Qudama, that Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan imposed retaliation
against a man who killed a mawla with a stick and so the mawla's
patron killed the man with a stick.


Malik said, ""The
generally agreed on way of doing things in our community about which
there is no dispute is that when a man strikes another man with a
stick or hits him with a rock or intentionally strikes him causing his
death, that is an intentional injury and there is retaliation for it.""


Malik said, ""Intentional murder with us is that a man
intentionally goes to a man and strikes him until his life goes. Part
of intentional injury also is that a man strikes a man in a quarrel
between them. He leaves him while he is alive, and he bleeds to death
and so dies. There is retaliation for that.""


Malik said,
""What is done in our community is that a group of free men are killed
for the intentional murder of one free man, and a group of women for
one woman, and a group of slaves for one slave."""
"1712.2","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab that Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf said"
"1713.1","Yahya narrated to me from Malik that it reached him that Marwan ibn al-Hakam wrote to Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan mentioning that a drunkard who had killed a man was brought to him. Mu'awiyah wrote back: ""Kill him for it."" Yahya said: Malik said: The best interpretation I have heard for this verse — Allah's words: {The free for the free, the slave for the slave, and the female for the female} (2:178) — is that these are the males, {and the female for the female} means qisas (retaliation) is between females as it is between males. A free woman is killed for a free woman as a free man is killed for a free man; a slave woman is killed for a slave woman as a slave is killed for a slave. Qisas is between women as it is between men, and qisas is also between men and women. Allah says in His Book: {And We ordained for them therein: life for life, eye for eye, nose for nose, ear for ear, tooth for tooth, and wounds equal for equal} (5:45). Allah mentions life for life, so the life of a free woman is for the life of a free man, and her wound for his wound. Malik said concerning a man who holds a man for another man who strikes him and he dies on the spot: if he held him knowing he intended to kill him, both are killed for it. If he held him thinking he only intended to strike as people strike, not intending to kill, the killer is killed and the holder is severely punished and imprisoned for a year, because he held him, but there is no killing on him. Malik said concerning a man who kills a man intentionally or gouges his eye intentionally: the killer is killed or the gouger's eye is gouged."
"1713.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Humayd ibn Qays al-Makki said"
