"1762.1","[1762] On the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, that Rafi’ bin Ishaq, the client of Al-Shifa’, informed him, he said: Abd and I entered We will return to him, and Abu Sa’id said to us: The Messenger of God, peace and blessings of God be upon him, informed us: Angels do not enter a house in which there are statues or pictures. Ishaq doubted, he did not know whether they were orphans. Abu Sa`id said: Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 1762 Arabic Hadith:"
"1762.2","[1762] On the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, that Rafi’ bin Ishaq, the client of Al-Shifa’, informed him, he said: Abd and I entered We will return to him, and Abu Sa’id said to us: The Messenger of God, peace and blessings of God be upon him, informed us: Angels do not enter a house in which there are statues or pictures. Ishaq doubted, he did not know whether they were orphans. Abu Sa`id said: Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 1762 Arabic Hadith:"
"1763.1","[1763] On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masoud, that he entered upon Abu Talha al-Ansari to visit him, He said: He found Saul bin Hanif with him, so Abu Talha called a man and he removed a pattern from underneath him, and Saul bin Hanif said to him: Why do you take it off? He said: Because it contains images, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about it what you already know. Sahil said: Didn’t the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Except what was a pattern on a garment. He said: Yes, but it is better for myself.\\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 1763 Arabic Hadith:"
"1763.2","[1763] On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masoud, that he entered upon Abu Talha al-Ansari to visit him, He said: He found Saul bin Hanif with him, so Abu Talha called a man and he removed a pattern from underneath him, and Saul bin Hanif said to him: Why do you take it off? He said: Because it contains images, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about it what you already know. Sahil said: Didn’t the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Except what was a pattern on a garment. He said: Yes, but it is better for myself.\\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 1763 Arabic Hadith:"
