"1788.2","Malik related to me from Humayd at-Tawil that Anas ibn Malik said"
"1789.1","Malik related to me that he heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"1789.2","From Abu al-Sa'ib, mawla of Hisham ibn Zuhrah, that he said: I entered upon Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and found him praying. I sat waiting until he finished. I heard a rustling under a bed in his house — a snake. I stood to kill it. Abu Sa'id gestured to me to sit. When he finished, he gestured to a room in the house and said: ""Do you see this house?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""There was a young man in it, recently married. He went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to the Trench. While he was there, the young man asked permission: 'O Messenger of Allah, permit me to visit my family.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) permitted him and said: 'Take your weapon, for I fear Banu Qurayzah for you.' The young man went to his family and found his wife standing between the two doors. He lunged at her with his spear to stab her, but a ghayrah (protective jealousy) overtook her. She said: 'Do not hasten until you enter and see what is in your house.' He entered and found a snake coiled on his bed. He thrust his spear into it, then came out with it and planted it in the courtyard. The snake thrashed on the spearhead, and the young man fell dead. It was not known which died first, the young man or the snake. This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: 'In Medina there are jinn who have become Muslim. If you see any of them, give them three days' notice. If they appear after that, kill them, for they are devils.'"" Muwatta Imam Malik, Hadith 1789."
