"1804.2","Malik related to me that he heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab went to the villages every Saturday. If he found a slave doing work which he was not capable of doing"
"1805.1","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a disbelieving guest was hosted by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered a sheep to be milked for him, and he drank its milk. Then another was milked, and he drank its milk. Then another was milked, and he drank its milk, until he drank the milk of seven sheep. The next morning, he became Muslim. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered a sheep to be milked for him, and he drank its milk. Then he ordered another to be milked, but he did not finish it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The believer drinks in one intestine"
"1805.2","It was narrated from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever says to his brother"
