"1813.2","Malik related to me from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"1814.1","Malik narrated to me from Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: Abu Talhah said to Umm Sulaym: ""I heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) weak, and I recognized hunger in it. Do you have anything?"" She said: ""Yes."" She brought out barley loaves, took her khimar, wrapped the bread in part of it, tucked it under my hand, wrapped me in part of it, and sent me to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). I went and found the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sitting in the mosque with people. I stood over them. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Did Abu Talhah send you?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""For food?"" I said: ""Yes."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to those with him: ""Rise."" They rose, and I went ahead of them until I came to Abu Talhah and informed him. Abu Talhah said: ""O Umm Sulaym, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has come with people, and we have no food to feed them."" She said: ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" Abu Talhah went out to meet the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came with Abu Talhah until they entered. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Bring what you have, O Umm Sulaym."" She brought that bread. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered it to be crumbled, and Umm Sulaym squeezed her small leather flask of clarified butter over it, making a broth. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said what Allah willed, then said: ""Permit ten to enter."" He permitted them; they ate until full, then left. Then he said: ""Permit ten."" He permitted them; they ate until full, then left. Then he said: ""Permit ten."" He permitted them; they ate until full, then left. Then he said: ""Permit ten."" He permitted them; they ate until full, then left. Then he said: ""Permit ten."" He permitted them; they ate until full, then left. Until all the people had eaten and were satisfied. The people were seventy or eighty men."
