"1835.1","Malik narrated to me from Sadaqah ibn Yasar that he said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab about wearing a ring. He said: ""Wear it, and inform people that I gave you a fatwa to that effect."""
"1835.2","From Abu al-Hubab Sa'id ibn Yasar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever gives charity from pure earnings — and Allah accepts only what is pure — it is as if he places it in the Hand of the Most Merciful, Who nurtures it as one of you nurtures his foal or young camel, until it becomes like a mountain."" Muwatta Imam Malik, Hadith 1835."
